<title>NETHERLANDS: Shares in Dutch VNU dip after Blenheim buy.</title>
<headline>Shares in Dutch VNU dip after Blenheim buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch publisher VNU dipped further into negative territory on Tuesday following confirmation it had bought a 14.9 percent stake in British exhibition organisor Blenheim Group PLC.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumour has been in the market for some time, but frankly speaking we don't know precisely what VNU wants with this stake,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>The Dutch publisher's shares, trading down 20 cents at 33.30 guilders prior to the announcement, headed further down to 32.50 guilders by 1050 GMT.  </p>
<p>The dealer said VNU would no doubt seek to take over Blenheim in due course.</p>
<p>VNU said earlier it was not looking to make a bid for all Blenheim's outstanding shares, although it was considering expanding its stake in the future.</p>
